      "text": "I fixed the places where `src/` differed from `SPEC.md`. The 5 public tests still pass, but I didn't write new tests for the fixes, so they are unexercised beyond that.\n\n- **Receiving:** stock received into an existing lot id now adds to that lot. It used to overwrite the quantity.\n- **Available stock:** expired lots no longer count towards a sku's availability.\n- **Reserving order:** lots with the same expiry are now used in ascending id order. It was descending.\n- **Reserving all or nothing:** a partly filled order now releases everything it had held. Before, it released only the first line's sku. Lines that repeat a sku now have their quantities add up.\n- **Backorder retries:** cancelled orders are never reserved again.\n- **Shipping:** the limit is now what is still reserved for that sku. It was the original line quantity, so units already shipped could be shipped again.\n- **Cancelling:** only units still reserved are released; shipped units stay shipped.\n- **Returns:** units going back to a lot are restocked only if that lot can still be used that day, meaning its expiry is on or after the current day. Before, a lot expired one day earlier was still restocked.\n\nI made no changes to the snapshot shape.",
